1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,127
Welcome to the third episode of Earthlings 101, the crash course for alien visitors.

2
00:00:05,475 --> 00:00:06,835
Let's talk about sex!

3
00:00:43,135 --> 00:00:44,699
So, what is sex?

4
00:00:44,942 --> 00:00:48,282
Most species on earth are divided into male and female specimen.

5
00:00:48,765 --> 00:00:54,561
Sexual reproduction is a process where a male and a female individual combine their genetic code to create a new individual.

6
00:00:54,942 --> 00:00:56,071
How does this work?

7
00:00:56,326 --> 00:00:58,554
Consider a couple of typical earth animals.

8
00:00:58,554 --> 00:01:04,494
Most of their cells contain a double set of DNA: one from the male parent, and one from the female one.

9
00:01:04,834 --> 00:01:14,691
To be able to reproduce, both male and female create cells containing only one randomly mixed set of DNA: Then the male injects his cells into the female, a process called copulation.

10
00:01:15,192 --> 00:01:26,692
One male cell fusionates with the female one and creates a full fledged cell with the usual double set of DNA: This cell is the base for the new organism which starts now growing - either in an egg, or inside the body of the female.

11
00:01:29,932 --> 00:01:35,832
Note that the DNA of the parents isn't mixed to one set of DNA until the new specimen creates its sex cells.

12
00:01:36,492 --> 00:01:40,935
That's why on earth, different species can interbreed but the offspring won't be able to reproduce.

13
00:01:42,201 --> 00:01:43,276
Scientific advice.

14
00:01:43,634 --> 00:01:49,140
If you want to use human biology to build bio-computers, don't limit your research to the brain.

15
00:01:49,522 --> 00:01:54,795
During copulation, a male human ejaculates about 300 million sperm cells within 5 seconds.

16
00:01:55,296 --> 00:02:00,773
The DNA in each cell consists of 3 billion base pairs, each one storing 2 bits of information.

17
00:02:00,773 --> 00:02:09,233
This means that a human ejaculation has a bandwidth of about 40000 terabytes/sec, which is twelve times more than the bitrate of Xelarian neuro-cables.

18
00:02:09,813 --> 00:02:13,455
Female earthlings carry their children inside their body for nine moon cycles.

19
00:02:13,941 --> 00:02:20,450
During this time, they can't make other children, while the males can run around, hunt, fight, and copulate with other women.

20
00:02:20,450 --> 00:02:25,610
So the bottleneck for population growth in a tribe is the number of females, not the number of males.

21
00:02:26,270 --> 00:02:30,466
That's why men are traditionally the hunters and fighters and protect women and children with their life.

22
00:02:31,346 --> 00:02:35,855
Males are dispensable - even a single male can impregnate a whole tribe of females.

23
00:02:36,737 --> 00:02:39,477
The question is: why do earthlings have sex?

24
00:02:39,817 --> 00:02:49,394
The answer lies in the human mind, as I explained it in the first episode: the beast pushes the ego to have sex with a feeling called desire, and reward sex with another feeling called pleasure.

25
00:02:49,394 --> 00:02:54,834
The niggler, on the other side, enforces rules of society through feelings like shame and guilt.

26
00:02:55,554 --> 00:02:58,768
Most human behaviour comes from this power game between beast and niggler.

27
00:02:59,415 --> 00:03:06,265
But in case of sexuality, the beast disposes of a trump card: Love, a strong feeling to emotionally attach the human to another earthling.

28
00:03:06,667 --> 00:03:11,050
Love feels good, and right and noble, and is immune to both reason and remorse.

29
00:03:11,510 --> 00:03:15,495
So, earthlings think that acting out of love is an excuse for pretty much anything.

30
00:03:15,495 --> 00:03:23,935
In the last episode, we have seen that life on earth, from photosynthesis to human civilization, is all about one thing: Spreading the genetic code.

31
00:03:24,315 --> 00:03:26,303
We might call this the "genetic imperative".

32
00:03:26,754 --> 00:03:29,288
But why did the genetic imperative favour sex?

33
00:03:29,720 --> 00:03:35,469
Wouldn’t it be more efficient if all specimen could bear children on their own, without complicated mating rituals and copulation?

34
00:03:35,873 --> 00:03:39,195
The answer may lie in a somewhat special kind of creatures: parasites.

35
00:03:40,496 --> 00:03:47,636
Actually, parasites exist only on earth, because it's the only planet where the anti-parasite regulations of the Central Bureaucracy don't apply.

36
00:03:47,916 --> 00:03:54,321
Of course, those regulations don't hold for brain suckers, but that's only because brain suckers kinda run the bureaucracy.

37
00:03:54,701 --> 00:03:57,987
Therefore they are legally not considered parasites but "authoritarian symbionts".

38
00:03:59,388 --> 00:04:07,905
Parasites are usually small creatures - like insects, microbes or worms - which live on, or even inside bigger creatures, draining their resources.

39
00:04:08,426 --> 00:04:14,247
The problem is that parasites grow and reproduce faster than their hosts, so they can adapt to any mutation of the host.

40
00:04:14,732 --> 00:04:20,012
So, fighting parasites by mutating is useless, because the parasites can mutate much faster.

41
00:04:20,012 --> 00:04:24,172
But sexually reproducing animals show huge differences with each generation.

42
00:04:24,572 --> 00:04:29,016
So it's much harder for parasites to adapt to the ever-changing characteristics of their hosts.

43
00:04:29,557 --> 00:04:33,925
So, in a world with gazillions of parasites, sexuality is a better strategy.

44
00:04:34,406 --> 00:04:37,206
That's why sexuality is so popular on earth.

45
00:04:37,606 --> 00:04:39,353
Almost all species do it...

46
00:04:39,654 --> 00:04:41,774
Except for the microbes.

47
00:04:44,374 --> 00:04:45,732
Tips for tourists.

48
00:04:45,732 --> 00:04:51,352
If you want to observe human sexual behaviour, look for urban zones called red light districts.

49
00:04:51,832 --> 00:04:59,202
You might not be able to observe an actual copulation, but you may see human mating-dances and watch educational films about sexual reproduction.

50
00:05:00,044 --> 00:05:04,544
Now, the interesting thing about sex is that it alters completely the rules of evolution.

51
00:05:04,884 --> 00:05:06,144
Why is this so?

52
00:05:06,424 --> 00:05:11,400
Well, in natural selection, the most successful individuals are those who are able to survive.

53
00:05:11,400 --> 00:05:16,340
So, when a mutation is successful, it's usually because it serves a certain purpose.

54
00:05:16,720 --> 00:05:22,590
But sexual reproduction involves picking a mate, and evolution pushes the individuals to be picky about their mates.

55
00:05:22,953 --> 00:05:27,555
In general, female animals are pickier because they have a limited reproduction capacity.

56
00:05:27,858 --> 00:05:29,658
This is called sexual selection.

57
00:05:30,143 --> 00:05:36,335
So, sexiness - the ability to attract possible mates - becomes an important factor for evolutionary success.

58
00:05:36,335 --> 00:05:43,595
This situation creates some sort of "strange loop": one of the most important factors in sexiness is actually: sexiness.

59
00:05:44,395 --> 00:05:48,363
Consider a group of animals where some males have a tiny tentacle growing out of their head.

60
00:05:48,729 --> 00:05:51,195
Let's assume some females find this rather cute.

61
00:05:51,745 --> 00:05:54,745
So, males with tentacles become slightly sexier.

62
00:05:55,145 --> 00:06:04,577
The point is, sexy males are likely to have sexy offspring, and every female wants sexy offspring, because the sexier the offspring is, the more he will spread mummy's genetic code.

63
00:06:04,577 --> 00:06:11,037
In consequence, even the females who were not interested in tentacles in the first place want now sexy tentaculous offspring.

64
00:06:11,457 --> 00:06:14,237
So, tentacles become even more attractive.

65
00:06:14,557 --> 00:06:23,045
So we have entered a strange loop where tentacles are sexy simply because tentacles are sexy, without any practical reason other than the fact that everybody wants sexy offspring.

66
00:06:23,467 --> 00:06:30,108
From generation to generation, tentacles will grow bigger and bigger until they are so encumbering that they actually reduce the ability to survive.

67
00:06:30,108 --> 00:06:33,148
This example is less exaggerated than it seems.

68
00:06:33,628 --> 00:06:39,765
Some species develop giant encumbering antlers, or huge colored tail feathers, or elaborate mating songs.

69
00:06:42,488 --> 00:06:50,500
Some scientists even think that human intelligence has developed as kind of "mental antlers", pushed forward by sexual selection rather than by the need for survival.

70
00:06:50,500 --> 00:06:53,440
Now let's have a closer look at earthling sexuality.

71
00:06:53,760 --> 00:06:55,920
When are earthlings considered to be attractive?

72
00:06:56,580 --> 00:07:05,581
Males are attractive when they are strong, healthy, aggressive and intelligent, and have a high social rank, because all this means that they will be able to protect and feed their mate and offspring.

73
00:07:05,581 --> 00:07:13,981
Also, a male who spreads his DNA pretty much anywhere is sexy, because in this case, chances are that his sons will spread mummy's DNA pretty much anywhere.

74
00:07:14,441 --> 00:07:27,621
And finally, males should not be so old that they are likely to die within some years, because then they won't be able to protect and feed their offspring - except if they are old and rich, which means that they will leave a lot of money behind, and money can buy protection and food.

75
00:07:27,621 --> 00:07:30,609
So, old men are only sexy if they are rich.

76
00:07:30,910 --> 00:07:36,890
For females, the primary selection criterion is the ability to bear a lot of children before she runs out of egg cells.

77
00:07:37,410 --> 00:07:39,579
So, health and youth are crucial.

78
00:07:39,951 --> 00:07:43,644
Large hips are sexy because large hip bones make childbearing easier.

79
00:07:44,085 --> 00:07:49,385
Also, a slim waist is sexy because it means that the large hips don't just come from an excess of body fat.

80
00:07:49,785 --> 00:07:54,468
And finally, large breasts are sexy because, well, nobody really knows why.

81
00:07:54,468 --> 00:08:01,568
They may just have evolved by the strange loop of sexual selection, without any particular reason, like antlers or colored tail feathers.

82
00:08:01,888 --> 00:08:06,128
And finally, intelligence and social rank also add to the attractivity.

83
00:08:07,808 --> 00:08:09,172
Strategic advice.

84
00:08:09,172 --> 00:08:17,331
If you want to infiltrate human society with shape shifters to gather intelligence for an invasion, you may consider your operatives taking the shape of attractive females.

85
00:08:17,331 --> 00:08:25,853
If you do so, pay attention to details: Even minor errors like the wrong number of eyes or the wrong skin color may freak out humans and compromise your agents.

86
00:08:27,214 --> 00:08:33,954
Spreading the code and choosing partners with quality DNA are not the only goals: The humans must also feed and protect their offspring.

87
00:08:34,371 --> 00:08:40,293
Humans usually unite those goals by choosing one long-term partner to raise the children with - and then cheating upon him.

88
00:08:40,293 --> 00:08:49,063
For a male earthling, a proven strategy is to choose one female as long-term partner, and then copulate with lots of other females behind her back to spread the code.

89
00:08:49,645 --> 00:08:54,355
Society tolerates this behaviour, more or less, and a man who does so is considered a winner.

90
00:08:55,277 --> 00:09:01,057
Women, on the other hand, usually carry one child at a time, no matter how many sexual partners they have.

91
00:09:01,057 --> 00:09:04,539
So they better be picky about the DNA of their children's fathers.

92
00:09:05,007 --> 00:09:08,537
That's why society frowns upon women who have a lot of sexual partners.

93
00:09:08,950 --> 00:09:18,695
A popular female strategy is to choose the best possible long-term partner, to feed and protect her offspring - and then cheat upon him with another male providing high-quality DNA for said offspring.

94
00:09:19,116 --> 00:09:24,897
This is often one of the "winners" we mentioned before, or at least a younger, richer or otherwise more attractive male.

95
00:09:24,897 --> 00:09:30,297
Of course, no male wants to raise the offspring of a rival, so the cheating has to be done in secret.

96
00:09:30,737 --> 00:09:37,257
Again, this behaviour is often more or less tolerated by society, or even romantically idealized in fictional works.

97
00:09:37,577 --> 00:09:46,777
Speaking of fictional works: vampires, the fictional predators mentioned in episode one, are considered highly attractive, because they are real experts in feeding and not dying.

98
00:09:47,257 --> 00:09:53,451
There is even a popular fictional work about an underage girl having a relationship with a vampire who has more than six times her age.

99
00:09:53,451 --> 00:10:00,528
A relationship between humans having this age difference would never be tolerated by society, but apparently it's ok if the male is a vampire.

100
00:10:00,849 --> 00:10:06,836
It should be mentioned that many animal species have developed same sex copulation, also known as homosexuality.

101
00:10:07,098 --> 00:10:13,018
This has nothing to do with reproduction, it serves social purposes, for example to resolve social conflicts.

102
00:10:13,418 --> 00:10:20,318
So it is all natural that some humans also show homosexual behaviour - except for creationists who claim not to descend from animals.

103
00:10:22,598 --> 00:10:27,994
When earthlings have raised children, one of their main concerns is often that the offspring keeps spreading the code.

104
00:10:28,257 --> 00:10:46,886
They push their children to look for partners with high-quality DNA, they encourage them to reproduce, and even tolerant parents tend to freak out if ever a child reveals as homosexual, simply because homosexual offspring is a dead end for the DNA: By the way, the fear of having homosexual offspring is the main reason why many earthlings think homosexuality is wrong.

105
00:10:47,226 --> 00:11:00,269
Human sexual behaviour, like human behaviour in general, is mostly determined by genetic programmation - either directly by human nature, or indirectly by society, which has evolved with human nature and is hard-wired into the human brain.

106
00:11:00,269 --> 00:11:08,149
After all, everything comes down to the single most important driving force of human civilization, the genetic imperative: Spreading the code.

107
00:11:08,529 --> 00:11:14,645
In the next episode we will talk about ethics: what is good, what is evil, and what has it all to do with eating fruits.

108
00:11:14,645 --> 00:11:19,791
We will also discuss what happens when you throw Mighty Cthulhu and Great Xenu together in prison.

109
00:11:20,912 --> 00:11:22,047
Thanks for watching.

